---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
---

<Page title="Privacy — Redmi Buds Bar">
  <main id="main" class="prose">
    <h1>
      Your listening.
      <br />
      <em>Your business.</em>
    </h1>
    <p>
      Redmi Buds Bar has no accounts, analytics, advertising, or audio
      recording.
    </p>
    <h2>Bluetooth</h2>
    <p>
      The app communicates locally with your paired REDMI Buds 8 Pro to read
      battery levels and change noise controls. It does not upload Bluetooth
      data.
    </p>
    <h2>Automatic updates</h2>
    <p>
      Sparkle checks the update feed at buds.robin.build and downloads signed
      releases from GitHub. Those services receive ordinary connection
      information, such as your IP address. You can disable automatic updates in
      the app’s settings.
    </p>
    <h2>Local diagnostics</h2>
    <p>
      A diagnostic log on your Mac contains protocol packets and connection
      status, never audio. It resets when the app starts and is capped at
      approximately 256 KB. You choose whether to share it when reporting a
      problem.
    </p>
    <h2>This website</h2>
    <p>
      The website is hosted by Cloudflare. It sets no analytics cookies and
      loads its fonts locally. Cloudflare processes ordinary request information
      to serve and protect the site.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a href="https://github.com/robin-liquidium/redmi-buds-bar">
        Read the source on GitHub ↗
      </a>
    </p>
  </main>
</Page>
